clean_summary:
Very cool talk about the future and the past of information retrieval. The speaker is pleased to see some of their contributions being mentioned.

@bclavie: "Information Retrieval is about making knowledge accessible. Late Interaction is the best way to do that today. But now that we have a new kind of users, it's time to zoom out so we can plan the future of retrieval. I gave a talk about this at @ir_tsukuba."

The linked slides discuss IR paradigms, including ColBERT and Late Interaction Retrieval, and explore future directions for the field.

